<LegalLayout
  title="Terms — NearPay"
  description="NearPay terms of service. Draft pending legal review."
  heading="Terms of service"
  updated="2026-11-07"
>
  <p>
    These terms are a draft for the NearPay preview. They are not yet in force and will be replaced by reviewed terms
    before NearPay is generally available.
  </p>
  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    NearPay provides software that lets merchants accept payments that settle directly to a destination they control.
    NearPay is non-custodial: it does not hold, pay out or reverse funds, and keys held by NearPay can only pay network
    fees or relay payments the owner has already signed.
  </p>
  <h2>Merchant responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide accurate business details. Live mode turns on when you save them; NearPay does not review or verify them, and may suspend or decline a business for abuse or where it cannot offer service.</li>
    <li>Keep control of your settlement destination and the wallet that signs refunds.</li>
    <li>Fulfil orders only after NearPay reports a payment as complete, which happens after settlement evidence is seen.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Route providers</h2>
  <p>
    Cross-chain payments are routed through third-party providers on NEAR Intents. Their terms require, among other things,
    that merchants are reviewed and that payer addresses are screened. The final terms will set out these flow-down
    provisions in full.
  </p>
  <h2>Fees</h2>
  <p>Fees are described in the <a href="/#pricing">pricing section</a> of the home page. They are indicative during the preview.</p>
</LegalLayout>
